Package: hullBase
Title: Rubberband Baseline Correction with Automatic Local Bending
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Thanya", "Manivannan", email = "thanyamanivannan@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Corrects the baseline of spectra, such as Fourier transform
    infrared (FTIR) spectra, using the rubberband (lower convex hull)
    method. A rubberband baseline cannot follow concave regions of the
    background. This package detects hull segments that hide a concave
    region and corrects each one by bending it locally before taking the
    hull, extending the manual bending approach described by Beleites
    (2015). Where to bend and how strongly are calculated from the
    spectrum's own noise level, so the only user setting is the expected
    peak width.
